---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {box,compact,roots,titles} from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="Home"><section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Chicago public money, one box at a time</p><h1>Where does the money go?</h1><p class="lede">A budget is a plan for how public money will be spent. Pick a government, then open a box to see what is inside. Every number has a source.</p><form action="/find" role="search"><label for="home-search">Find a school, park, department or box</label><div><input class="search-field" id="home-search" name="q" type="search" placeholder="Try police, parks or a school"/><button type="submit">Find</button></div></form></section><section aria-labelledby="budgets"><h2 id="budgets">Choose a budget</h2><div class="grid">{roots.map(root=><a class="card card-link" href={`/${root}`}><span class="eyebrow">2026 budget</span><h3>{titles[root]}</h3><span class="amount">{box(root)?compact(box(root)!.amount_cents):'Explore the budget'}</span><p>Open the boxes inside →</p></a>)}</div></section><section class="hero"><h2>How to read this</h2><p>Some numbers are printed in the budget. Others are estimates, leftovers or money paid so far. Their labels tell you which is which.</p><p><a href="/glossary">Learn the words</a> · <a href="/about">How we built this</a> · <a href="/gaps">What we could not find</a></p></section></Base>
